/// A failed call: what it returned and the message bfr_get_last_error gave for it, held in
/// place so a failure allocates nothing.
struct Error {
    Result code{};
    detail::Message message;
};

/// What a call returns: its value, or why it failed.
template <class T>
using Expected = std::expected<T, Error>;

/// Receives BFR's messages and validation's. Without one, BFR prints nothing. Called on any thread,
/// including threads BFR or the driver owns, until the instance and every device made from it are
/// destroyed. May be called on several threads at once.
/// message: Valid only during the call.
using MessageCallback = void (*)(MessageSeverity severity, std::string_view message, void* userData);

